+### Pinned Tab Chips
+
+- Description: Whether pinned tabs are rendered as compact, borderless chips that hug their contents.
+- Setting: `pinned_tab_chips`
+- Default: `false`
+
+**Options**
+
+`boolean` values
+
+Open the Settings Editor and choose **Edit in settings.json**. This option is
+configured in JSON:
+
+```json [settings]
+{
+  "tab_bar": {
+    "pinned_tab_chips": true
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Unpinned Tab Chips
+
+- Description: Whether unpinned tabs are rendered as compact, borderless chips that hug their contents.
+- Setting: `unpinned_tab_chips`
+- Default: `false`
+
+**Options**
+
+`boolean` values
+
+Open the Settings Editor and choose **Edit in settings.json**. This option is
+configured in JSON:
+
+```json [settings]
+{
+  "tab_bar": {
+    "unpinned_tab_chips": true
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Maximum Tab Rows
+
+- Description: Maximum number of rows for unpinned editor and terminal tabs (and the agent panel's threads and terminals row when `agent.threads_sidebar.in_agent_panel` is enabled). Wrapping is active only when both `tabs.min_width` and `tabs.max_width` are set; tabs fill up to `max_tab_rows` rows at `min_width` before the last row scrolls horizontally. `0` behaves as `1`.
+- Setting: `max_tab_rows`
+- Default: `1`
+
+**Options**
+
+Positive integer values (`1` or greater; `0` behaves as `1`).
+
+Open the Settings Editor and choose **Edit in settings.json**. This option is
+configured in JSON:
+
+```json [settings]
+{
+  "tabs": {
+    "min_width": 120,
+    "max_width": 200
+  },
+  "tab_bar": {
+    "max_tab_rows": 3
+  }
+}
+```
+
